As an aside, Fire, Lightening, and Digging all identify themselves
before you are required to type what you want to engrave.  When I'm
doing a mass wand ID session, I prefer to use my own unique messages
(as opposed to Elbereth) so I can more easily identify Teleportation. 
So I engrave my message with my fingers, then I engrave with a wand. 
If the wand doesn't identify itself immediately, I go ahead and wipe
out the message to write another unique one.  This probably isn't
strictly necessary, I could just add to the message, but at this point
it doesn't matter.  All the wands that rely on a message being there
already will have identified themselves by now, and it saves me a turn
of wiping out "Elbereth" and writing my unique message again.
I've become really anal about turn counts, but when you see a fast q
leaping twoards you all of a sudden....


